---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Home">
  <section class="hero container">
    <span class="badge">Free · Open source · Local-first</span>
    <h1>Practice Kubernetes like a DevOps engineer</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Structured labs, command drills, and troubleshooting scenarios — from Docker basics to
      observability. Run real workloads on your machine. No shared cloud clusters. No surprise bills.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/labs/">Start Lab 01</a>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="https://github.com/Jacob-Idolor/Pet_Projects/tree/main/kubernetes">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container card-grid">
    <article class="card">
      <h3>🐳 Docker foundations</h3>
      <p>Build images, debug containers, multi-stage Dockerfiles — before you touch kubectl.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>☸ 8 hands-on labs</h3>
      <p>Pods → Deployments → Services → Ingress → Storage → RBAC → Helm → monitoring.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>🔧 Break/fix drills</h3>
      <p>Intentionally broken YAML. Practice CrashLoopBackOff, missing endpoints, and more.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h3>📊 Observability</h3>
      <p>Prometheus, Grafana, runbooks — skills that transfer to Dynatrace and SRE work.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong>Local only:</strong> Lab manifests apply to <em>your</em> kind/minikube cluster — never a paid multi-tenant cloud lab.
        This site is static content; your AWS bill stays ~$1–5/mo if you host it yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
